  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of employers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Most of the industries and business owners have left the country. In the last biennium the Federation with ILO support regained visibility and introduced governance mechanisms and consultative processes leading to the definition of a 2-year Strategic Plan. Most of the actions of these business plans have been implemented under these difficult circumstances. Nevertheless, the Federation still needs to work to increase its capacity to regularly analyze the business environment and produce reports on policy issues. This needs to be encompassed with a sustainability strategy aiming to capacitate and increase its team working on policy topics. 
ILO will support the efforts of the Federation to rethink its research model. After a workshop and capacity-building programme with the largest companies in the country, the ILO will define with the Federation a business model to support the Yemen Federation in research and advocacy, targeting mainly the relevance of the private sector as an actor for the sustainable economic recovery of the country.</narrative>
  </description>
